      "role": "user",
      "content": "those are okay, but they still feel a bit too \"heroic\" or \"artistic\"? like a rogue or a muse feels almost cool. \n\nwhat i'm actually getting from the team is a bit more of a... i don't know... a \"pest\" vibe? not in a mean way, but like a little creature that just pops up and makes a mess of things right when you're trying to be serious. it's less \"inspiring muse\" and more \"annoying little thing that's constantly tripping us up\" or \"stealing our focus\" while we're trying to get the morning sorted. \n\ncan you give me a few metaphors that capture that more \"nuisance\" or \"unwanted guest\" feeling? something that describes a small, chaotic entity that just won't stay in its lane?",
      "source": "evaluator"
